    "editorialMarkdown": "The intended approach is a Flood-fill DFS. Each unvisited land cell begins one island, then DFS marks every land cell reachable from it. Marking on arrival prevents a cell from being counted twice.\n\nThe one trap most solvers hit is exploring neighbours before marking: two paths can revisit the same cell and recurse forever.\n\nTime complexity is O(rows * columns), because each cell is changed once, and space complexity is O(rows * columns) in the worst case for the recursion stack.",
